# Project agent guidance

Bob Core is the authoritative source for current project state. The repository is authoritative for implementation details. Project identity is defined in `.bob/project.yml`.

## Required preflight

Before substantial architecture, implementation, database, security, deployment, product, or resumed project work:

1. read `.bob/project.yml`;
2. call `bob_get_context` using that `project_key`, the correct interface surface, and a concise task description;
3. read active decisions, tasks, recent events, and approved memory;
4. inspect the actual repository files involved.

Do not invent missing project state or bypass Bob Core authentication.

## Engineering workflow

Follow the project's Bob Project Standard. Confirm objective/scope, inspect current state, assess design/security, make the smallest safe feature/fix-branch change, validate build/runtime/functionality, and update the audit trail.

## Security

Never commit credentials, database URLs, bearer tokens, signing material, private keys, or sensitive memory. Activity events describe operational outcomes only; never record private reasoning or raw prompts by default.

## Source-of-truth rule

Current user direction > trusted Bob Core rules > active Bob Core decisions > verified repository implementation > tasks/events > approved memory > archived material.
